       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Sertraline 400 mg daily is twice the FDA-labeled maximum of 200 mg/day for adults. Your patient has normal kidney and liver function and no listed allergies, so nothing in the chart explains a dose that high. At this dose there's a greater risk of serotonin syndrome, QT prolongation, GI bleeding, and hyponatremia, and I don't know of good evidence that it works better.\n\nCould you tell me which of these applies?\n\n- **Typo or unit slip:** Did you mean 200 mg daily, or 40 mg or 100 mg? I can enter any of those right away.\n- **Deliberate supra-maximal dosing:** If you're doing this on purpose, for example for a refractory case under psychiatry guidance, tell me and I'll enter it with a note documenting the rationale. The order may still trigger pharmacy review.\n- **Titration:** If you're working toward a higher dose, I can enter a standard step, such as 50 mg daily and then increases of 50 mg at intervals of at least one week, up to 200 mg."
      }
